A PipeWire-native Roland REAC endpoint: a libpipewire-0.3 client that puts a REAC
fabric into the PipeWire graph as nodes. An original implementation of public,
reverse-engineered protocol facts (see the FreeREAC reac-protocol reference); no
third-party code is embedded directly in this repository.

It builds against and reuses these FreeREAC components:

  - libreac (https://github.com/FreeREAC/libreac) — RX/measure core, header
    <reac/reac.h>. Pulled as a meson subproject. GPL-3.0-or-later.

  - reac-aes67 (https://github.com/FreeREAC/reac-aes67) — the plain-LE decode
    core (src/reac_decode.c), AF_PACKET capture (src/reac_capture.c) and pcap
    reader (src/pcap_source.c), compiled in from a sibling checkout.
    GPL-3.0-or-later.

reac-aes67's decode core carries portions derived from obs-h8819-source,
Copyright (C) 2022 Norihiro Kamae <norihiro@nagater.net> (GPL-3.0-or-later); REAC
wire framing per github.com/per-gron/reacdriver (GPL-3.0). Those attributions
travel with that source.

